A('1963-04-bentre-conf', '1963-04', VH, 'Bến Tre. In early April the Provincial Committee holds an enlarged conference. Since the new year Saigon has swept nearly every district and set up 129 more strategic hamlets; the freed area is narrower, the armed force weak, the main force dispersed. The conference holds it wrong not to fight the sweeps by arms. It decides to train and arm the two main-force companies, add a third and a support company, make the signal, scout, sapper and engineer platoons companies, fix the commands, and sets the "Ấp Bắc" emulation drive of the Central Office\'s Military Committee for the province.', 'III, 268–69', when='Apr., early', place='ben-tre', also=['vietnam'], vis=True, check='the day; the history does not give the conference\'s place.')
A('1963-04-thanhphong', '1963-04', VH, 'Bến Tre. At the end of April and the start of May the province\'s military board takes Companies 1 and 2 of the main force to the Thạnh Phong base, Thạnh Phú district, to train: covered L-shaped bunkers, fire at helicopters and M113s, mobile attack and ambush from squad to company, on the model of Ấp Bắc.', 'III, 269–70', when='Apr., late', place='thanh-phong', also=OP, check='the day.')
A('1963-04-longhung', '1963-04', VH, 'Mỹ Tho. In mid-April Company 2 of Battalion 514 destroys a Saigon company on a sweep at Long Hưng; the people rise with it, kill three Self-Defense squads and break the strategic hamlets of Kim Sơn and Vĩnh Kim.', 'III, 264–65', when='Apr., mid', place='long-hung', also=OP, check='the day; the history dates it "at this time", the Thị Qua bridge attack of mid-April.')
A('1963-04-thanhtri', '1963-04', VH, 'Mỹ Tho. In mid-April Company 2 of Battalion 514 goes to Chợ Gạo and breaks the Thạnh Trị strategic hamlet area.', 'III, 265', when='Apr., mid', place='cho-gao', also=OP, check='the day.')
A('1963-04-longtrung', '1963-04', VH, 'Mỹ Tho. In mid-April Company 1 of Battalion 514 with the people of Long Trung and Long Tiên, Cai Lậy, breaks up a large part of the strategic hamlets and sends the families back to their old villages.', 'III, 265', when='Apr., mid', place='long-trung', also=OP, check='the day.')
A('1963-0716-trunghoa', '1963-07-16', VH, 'Mỹ Tho. The night of July 16 Company 2 of Battalion 514 raids the Trung Hòa concentration zone, Chợ Gạo, destroys a Civil Guard platoon and helps the people to break out and go home.', 'III, 266–67', place='trung-hoa', band_='night', also=OP)
A('1963-0717-onghau', '1963-07-17', VH, 'Mỹ Tho. July 17 Company 2 of Battalion 514 and Chợ Gạo district\'s force beat back a raid by a battalion of the Saigon 7th Division and two Civil Guard companies: 40 killed and a fighter-bomber shot down at the Ông Hậu bridge, Mỹ Tịnh An commune, by the history\'s count.', 'III, 267', place='cho-gao', also=OP)
A('1963-0620-namngan', '1963-06-20', VH, 'Kiến Tường. Saigon opens the second stage of Đức Thắng 23 along the Năm Ngàn canal, June 20. The Provincial Committee and military board order the main, local and guerrilla forces to lie in wait and strike the columns, hurting part of their force and means.', 'III, 273', place='nam-ngan-canal', also=OP, check='the American record not read; the stage\'s opening, the first being Mar. 19 ([[cal.1963-03-19.vietnam-hanoi]]).')
A('1963-09-cauvan', '1963-09', VH, 'Bến Tre. In September, with the main force\'s new Company 3 and Thạnh Phú\'s troops, a raid hurts Civil Guard Company 854 heavily at Cầu Ván, Giao Thạnh commune, and the people of some strategic hamlets of the district rise and break them.', 'III, 272', when='Sept.', place='cau-van', also=OP, check='the day; the history dates it "in the same time" as the Mỹ Nhơn and Sơn Phú fights of Sept. 2 and 9.')
